course: dictionary
lesson: 4720
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hop has more than one meaning, so you need the words around it to know which one is meant. In «Small birds such as sparrows hop and leave pairs of prints», the birds are moving in small jumps.
explain: The words after hop can also change its meaning. «Hop on» and «hop off» mean to get on or off a bus, bike or train quickly, so the sentence is about travel, not jumping.
explain: Josh writes «I was hopping for a sunny day». Swap in the meaning «jumping» and it makes no sense, so Josh must mean wishing. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Hop is a verb: hop, hops, hopped, hopping. It can also be a noun: a hop is one small jump.
fact: «Hop» means to jump on one foot, or to move in small jumps, like a rabbit, a frog or a bird.
fact: «Hop on» and «hop off» mean to get on or off a bus, bike or train quickly.
fact: Hops are also a plant used in making beer.
fact: In maths, counted jumps along a number line use hops: the number of hops times the length of each hop.
exercise: «Many desert animals, like hopping mice, get almost all their water from their food.» What does hopping mean here? | *Moving in small jumps | Sleeping under the sand | Swimming in the waterhole | Singing at dawn
exercise: Mia says «hop on the bus» means jumping on one foot. What does hop on mean here? | To jump on one foot | *To get on quickly | To stop and wait at the stop | To carry a heavy bag
exercise: In a story, a frog hops from lily pad to lily pad. What is the frog doing? | Floating still on the water | *Making small jumps | Digging a hole in the mud | Flying up into the trees
test: «First he hopped one yard; then he hopped three yards; then he hopped five yards.» What does hopped mean here? | *Jumped along in short bounds | Fell down into the river | Ate some food | Walked slowly across the bridge
test: Josh writes «I was hopping for a sunny day». What does hopping mean in his sentence? | Jumping on one leg | *Wishing | Running very fast | Dancing in the sun
exam: In «Red kangaroos can hop at over 50 kilometres per hour», which clue shows that hop means moving by springing jumps? | The word largest | *Kangaroos are animals that leap along | The word newborn | The number 50
